<title>GERMANY: German Hochtief cuts 1996 dividend.</title>
<headline>German Hochtief cuts 1996 dividend.</headline>
<dateline>ESSEN, Germany 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hochtief AG, Germany's second largest building group, said on Wednesday it proposed to pay a dividend of 1.20 marks per five-mark share for the 1996 year.</p>
<p>In 1995, it paid a 13.50 mark dividend for each of its then-priced 50-mark shares. Total dividend pay-out for 1996 would fall to 84 million marks in 1996 compared to the 94.5 million marks it distributed in 1995, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Hochtief said the dividend proposal took into account charges from restructuring and the continued weak domestic construction market. Set against that were strong profits being made in its international business, it added.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
